    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0735" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg715"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Burnley.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 26, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you, with a view
                    to her Majesty’s, government being acquainted with the facts, that, owing to the
                    recent hostile and piratical proceedings on the lakes lying between the United
                    States and her Majesty’s <pb facs="0736" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/> possessions,
                    it has been deemed necessary, for the present, to increase the observing force
                    of the United States on those lakes; that the arrangement is temporary, and will
                    be discontinued so soon as circumstances permit, and that the vessels to be
                    employed on that service are to be under instructions to respect British rights
                    in all cases.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c, &amp;c, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
